  "schema": "arcpuzzles-parametric-prototype-evidence-v1",
  "scope": "# Review \u2014 48fee61713bb parametric public batch order\nTask/source: `48fee61713bb` v4.1.0; production generator SHA-256 remains `7a43eacd6626e8c595ea24c4a7c75874d6e40993598f3cc75dfc3b58ffdb3a3b`.\nDefect \u2192 repair: public files were emitted in caller/private setting order; the prototype now projects a whole batch, rejects visible duplicates, sorts by visible SHA-256, validates all labels, then writes in that order.\nCompatibility: `write_episode` keeps its previous return shape and delegates to the new `write_episodes` path.\nChanged scope: prototype, focused parametric tests, prototype README, and current task notes only.\nAuthority: canonical JSONL and both materialized Racket programs are byte-identical to baseline; normalized canonical rule hash remains `88f9214cd87f`.\nChecks: selected-task suite **92 passed**; reversed-order fixture **passed** with **142 actual Racket executions**, 3 demonstrations and 4 distinct queries per setting.\nTickets: the pinned `38eaf32b0d29` audit witness reproduced through Racket; the `8b0844e3951e` `grid_h` API boundary failed closed as advertised.\nRemaining scoped failures: none. No new safety finding was created.\nLimits: no broad production battery or large census was run because production generation/rules were unchanged; the parameter variant remains proposed and is not approved or training-admitted.\nAssessment: routine prototype-only repair, source-bound and ready for maintainer replay. Final code review was a separate author self-review because this harness has no reviewer subagent.\n",
